+## Design Notes
+
+- **Ladder semantics (ruled A):** in-play = assigned lanes ∪ {Standard}; untouched pipes keep the catalog default preset (byte-stable no-QoS runs). `streaming→Express` alone → 2 lanes → 70/30; `streaming→Express` + `email→Best-effort` → 3 lanes → 50/30/20 (Express exactly 50% — matches the story's launchable example + the 3-lane golden). The ladder's 1-lane row (100%) applies to the all-assignments-on-Standard edge and stays data-driven regardless.
+- **Command evolution (ruled A):** `Cmd_Set_Emphasis{pipe, weights:[3]i32}` — same tag, LOG_VERSION 3→4. The panel still offers the named presets app-side (a preset is a weight set); the auto-ladder and the manual editor both write weights through this one path, so replay equality holds by construction. Harness `emphasis <preset>` lowers preset id → weights.
+- **Right-click dial retirement (decision):** right-click on a pipe now selects it and opens/refreshes the QoS panel (the dial's cycle action is removed; the panel's per-row lane buttons + preset chips replace cycling). Rationale: the dial's only job was cycling opaque presets; the panel shows the consequence of every choice. Documented in the PR.
+- **Legible fonts (user note, 2026-08-14):** the full font story is a later story; for now the panel uses the existing `draw_text` (raylib default) at legible sizes (≥14px), strong ink/ink_soft contrast on the cream canvas, and clear spacing. No non-ASCII literals (lint gate 6).
+- **`[ASSUMPTION]` (PR body):** harder-eras / advanced-mode gating of manual editing is a future knob — not built. 2-class MVP roster (email + streaming) — the 3-lane golden exercises both assignments.
