+# qos_auto.dem — Story 5.8 golden: the assignment-driven auto-reservation
+# split (user ruling 2026-08-14). Era-3 demand (email 4/tick res->res +
+# streaming 2/tick host->res) over the res->router->host backbone. At 3000ms
+# the player categorizes BOTH classes on pipe 1 (router->host): streaming ->
+# Express + email -> Best-effort, so the in-play lanes are {Express, Standard,
+# Best-effort} = 3 and the auto ladder reserves 50/30/20 — the app writes the
+# computed set through Cmd_Set_Emphasis (the `weights` directive pins the
+# SERIALIZED outcome; the ladder COMPUTATION itself is core-tested in
+# qos_test.odin). Standard stays reserved even with no Standard-rider (the
+# canon-safe floor — un-categorized types ride it). The T2 captures pin the
+# painted lanes visibly re-splitting: 1000ms = default balanced, 6000ms =
+# 50/30/20.
+# fixture qos = the 3-node fixture + residentials 3,4. Node ids: 0=res,
+# 1=router, 2=host, 3=res, 4=res. Pipe ids (draw order): 0=res-router,
+# 1=router-host.
+seed 3003
+run 15000ms
+era 3
+fixture qos
+expect hash stable
+at 100ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 100ms draw 3 1 standard
+at 100ms draw 4 1 standard
+at 3000ms lane 1 streaming express
+at 3000ms lane 1 email best_effort
+at 3000ms weights 1 50 30 20
+capture at 1000ms
+capture at 6000ms
